\strong{true} class, learned from the probabilities the calibration data give
to their own class. A set with exactly one class is accepted and
predicted as that class; an empty set is accepted and predicted as the
arg max; a set with several classes is rejected. The \code{score} is not
used, the calibration \code{truth} is required and the level \code{alpha} is the
error level of the sets (see \code{\link[=target_level]{target_level()}}); a coverage or metric
target is met by searching over \code{alpha}. The selector is not
monotone in \code{alpha} in general, so the grid point whose calibration
coverage is closest to the request is used.
}
